   "source": [
    "Analysis A: Detailed Statistics for Temperature&Uncertainty"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "7hauWFwJqqWf"
   },
   "source": [
    "This analysis aims to quantify the spread of temperature readings and, curcially, the realiability of those readings as measured by AverageTemperatureUncertainty column."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "ROlIaxKdqzt7",
    "outputId": "6be8e78a-9b33-4bf0-f8cd-df19459d9918"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "       AverageTemperature  AverageTemperatureUncertainty\n",
      "count        8.235082e+06                   8.235082e+06\n",
      "mean         1.672743e+01                   1.028575e+00\n",
      "std          1.035344e+01                   1.129733e+00\n",
      "min         -4.270400e+01                   3.400000e-02\n",
      "25%          1.029900e+01                   3.370000e-01\n",
      "50%          1.883100e+01                   5.910000e-01\n",
      "75%          2.521000e+01                   1.349000e+00\n",
      "max          3.965100e+01                   1.539600e+01\n",
      "\n",
      "Mean Uncertainty in 1800: 2.52°C\n",
      "Mean Uncertainty in 2000: 0.34°C\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Select key columns for analysis\n",
    "reliability_col = ['AverageTemperature','AverageTemperatureUncertainty']\n",
    "\n",
    "#Obtain descriptive statistics (Mean, SD, Min, Max, Percentile)\n",
    "stats_summ = temp_by_city[reliability_col].describe()\n",
    "print(stats_summ)\n",
    "\n",
    "#Compute correlation between time and uncertainty\n",
    "temp_by_city['year'] = temp_by_city['dt'].dt.year\n",
    "uncertainty_trend = temp_by_city.groupby('year')['AverageTemperatureUncertainty'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMean Uncertainty in 1800: {uncertainty_trend.loc[1800]:.2f}°C\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean Uncertainty in 2000: {uncertainty_trend.loc[2000]:.2f}°C\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "XKiJf6bxrjlw"
   },
   "source": [
    "Average Temperature"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "rq0dsQhqqYrM"
   },
   "source": [
    "As noted in the histogram visualisation, the global land temperature usually centers around 15-20°C. The describe() function typically reveals a wide range (e.g., -40°C to 50°C), capturing the extremes of polar and equatorial climates mentioned in the report.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "U46SM7MJrq69"
   },
   "source": [
    "Average Temperature Uncertainty\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "5mw7qLh-rtdd"
   },
   "source": [
    "This column represents the 95% confidence interval for the temperature measurement.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "In the early records (1700s-1800s), uncertainty values are expected to be significantly higher (often >2°C) due to less precise instruments, fewer stations, and interpolation challenges.\n",
    "\n",
    "As we approach the 21st century, the uncertainty values typically shrink (often <0.5°C), reflecting modern standardized meteorological practices. This validates the report's conclusion that recent data is more complete and reliable."
