  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This datasets contains of 6 sub-datasets per gases:\n",
    "- Country-level emissions by gas\n",
    "- Country-level emissions by gas and fuel\n",
    "- Country-level emissions by gas and sector\n",
    "- Global emissions by gas and fuel\n",
    "- Global emissions by gas and sector\n",
    "- Global emissions by gas, fuel and sector"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "M3Uh3-swGEaT"
   },
   "source": [
    "The emissions data for each gas are provided as separate .csv files with columns for country, units, and emission values by year. For convenience and efficiency in further analysis, we will combine them into a single consolidated file by merging the Dataframes based on year and country. This allows us to easily correlate emissions of different gases with weather patterns in our subsequent analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Country-level "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "AG_oQesyi0G5"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_path = ROOT + \"CEDS_v_2025_03_18_aggregate/\"\n",
    "bc = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"BC_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "ch4 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"CH4_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "co2 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"CO2_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "co = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"CO_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "n2o = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"N2O_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "nh3 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"NH3_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "nmvoc = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"NMVOC_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "nox = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"NOx_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "oc = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"OC_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "so2 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"SO2_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "H2KK_jr4ygEi"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dfs = [bc, ch4, co2, co, n2o, nh3, nmvoc, nox, oc, so2]\n",
    "long_dfs = []\n",
    "for df in dfs:\n",
    "    year_cols = [col for col in df.columns if col.startswith('X')]\n",
    "    df = df.drop(columns='units')\n",
    "    df_long = df.melt(id_vars=['em', 'country'],\n",
    "                      value_vars=year_cols,\n",
    "                      var_name='year', value_name='value')\n",
    "    df_long['year'] = df_long['year'].str[1:].astype(int)\n",
    "    long_dfs.append(df_long)\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3 = pd.concat(long_dfs, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3 = ds3.pivot(\n",
    "          index=['country', 'year'],\n",
    "          columns='em',\n",
    "          values='value'\n",
    "      ).reset_index()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "S9flLtk7GEaT"
   },
   "source": [
    "Now that we have the consolidated emissions dataset, we can perform data profiling to understand the distribution of emissions across different gases, identify any missing values or outliers, and explore trends over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "PyT90R3pGEaT"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3.head(5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "-Hdq1Tr7GEaT"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3.describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "pjf9BDgfGEaT"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3.info()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "HWkKTj1HGEaU"
   },
   "source": [
    "Final .csv file contains emissions data for 9 gases (BC, CH4, CO, CO2, N2O, NH3, NMVOC, NOx, OC, and SO2) across 221 countries from 1750 to 2023. The dataset is structured in a long format with columns for country, gas type, year, and emission values. This structure allows for flexible analysis of emissions trends by gas and by country over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ruF4-1uhGEaU"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Number of countries:\", ds3[\"country\"].nunique())\n",
    "total_years = ds3[\"year\"].nunique()\n",
    "print(\"Number of unique years:\", total_years)\n",
    "print(\"First year:\", ds3[\"year\"].min())\n",
    "print(\"Last year:\", ds3[\"year\"].max())\n",
    "\n",
    "years_per_country = ds3.groupby(\"country\")[\"year\"].nunique()\n",
    "incomplete_countries = years_per_country[years_per_country < total_years]\n",
    "if incomplete_countries.empty:\n",
    "    print(\"All countries have complete year coverage.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Countries with missing years:\")\n",
    "    print(incomplete_countries)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "IqHXP168GEaU"
   },
   "source": [
    "We found that dataset contains 221 countries spanning 274 years (1750-2023). All countries have no missing years in the data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "yuCsnwIRGEaU"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot total emissions of each gas over time\n",
    "emissions_over_time = ds3.groupby('year').sum(numeric_only=True)\n",
    "gases = emissions_over_time.columns.tolist()\n",
    "n = len(gases)\n",
    "ncols = 3\n",
    "nrows = n // ncols + 1\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axs = plt.subplots(nrows, ncols, figsize=(ncols * 4, nrows * 2.5))\n",
    "axs = axs.flatten()\n",
    "\n",
    "step = max(1, len(emissions_over_time) // 6)\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, gas in enumerate(gases):\n",
    "    ax = axs[i]\n",
    "    ax.plot(emissions_over_time.index, emissions_over_time[gas], label=gas, linewidth=0.9)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(gas, fontsize=9)\n",
    "    ax.set_xticks(emissions_over_time.index[::step])\n",
    "    ax.set_xticklabels(emissions_over_time.index[::step], rotation=45, fontsize=7)\n",
    "    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "    ax.tick_params(axis='both', which='major', labelsize=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "for j in range(len(gases), len(axs)):\n",
    "    axs[j].axis('off')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Total Emissions of Each Gas Over Time')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "597rq0RWGEaU"
   },
   "source": [
    "After plotting the emissions of each gas over time, we observed that some gas data (e.g., CH4 and N2O) only starts from the 20th century, while others have records dating back to the 18th century. This reflects historical measurement capabilities and highlights the importance of considering temporal coverage when analysing trends. We see that all gases show a huge increase in emissions, especially in the 20th century, which is consistent with the report's conclusion that industrialisation has led to a significant rise in greenhouse gas emissions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Amount of missing values per gas (==0 or NaN)\n",
    "missing_values = ((ds3 == 0) | (ds3.isnull())).sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Missing values per gas (NaN + 0):\")\n",
    "print(missing_values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "-mwmOuX0JABn"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# No null check\n",
    "avg_no_check = ds3.groupby('country').size().mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check all columns\n",
    "cols_all = ds3.columns.difference(['country', 'year'])\n",
    "valid_all = ((ds3[cols_all].notna()) & (ds3[cols_all] != 0)).all(axis=1)\n",
    "avg_check_all = ds3[valid_all].groupby('country').size().mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Exclude CH4 and N2O\n",
    "cols_excl = ds3.columns.difference(['country', 'year', 'CH4', 'N2O'])\n",
    "valid_excl = ((ds3[cols_excl].notna()) & (ds3[cols_excl] != 0)).all(axis=1)\n",
    "avg_excl = ds3[valid_excl].groupby('country').size().mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Exclude CH4, N2O, and additional columns (e.g., BC, OC)\n",
    "cols_excl_more = ds3.columns.difference(['country', 'year', 'CH4', 'N2O', 'CO2'])\n",
    "valid_excl_more = ((ds3[cols_excl_more].notna()) & (ds3[cols_excl_more] != 0)).all(axis=1)\n",
    "avg_excl_more = ds3[valid_excl_more].groupby('country').size().mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "labels = [\n",
    "    \"No Null Check\",\n",
    "    \"Check All Columns\",\n",
    "    \"Exclude CH4 & N2O\",\n",
    "    \"Exclude CH4, N2O, CO2\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "values = [\n",
    "    avg_no_check,\n",
    "    avg_check_all,\n",
    "    avg_excl,\n",
    "    avg_excl_more\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10,5))\n",
    "bars = plt.bar(labels, values)\n",
    "\n",
