   "source": [
    "## Data Preparation (Process)\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "xqBeFSZFJABn"
   },
   "source": [
    "### DS1 Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "As part of data preparation for DS1 (Earth Surface Temperature Data), we implement a series of transformation and profiling tasks to convert the raw city-level monthly temperature data into a clean, analysis-ready country-level yearly dataset. The transformation pipeline consists of three main operations: aggregation to convert monthly data to yearly averages, integration to roll up city-level data to country-level, and imputation to fill missing city values using country-level averages. We begin by profiling the missing value patterns to understand data quality issues, then apply these transformations sequentially. Finally, we profile the resulting dataset to verify the transformations and persistently store the prepared data for subsequent analysis phases."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_path = ROOT + \"/berkeley-temp/\"\n",
    "temp_by_city = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"GlobalLandTemperaturesByCity.csv\")\n",
    "temp_by_city['dt'] = pd.to_datetime(temp_by_city['dt'])\n",
    "print(temp_by_city.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "oJV9J91YJABn"
   },
   "source": [
    "#### Profiling of Missing Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Before applying transformations, we profile the missing value patterns to understand data quality issues and inform our imputation strategy. This profiling step helps us identify which time periods and regions have incomplete data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 887
    },
    "id": "u-g6HJ5rJABn",
    "outputId": "99657d57-c674-4075-f551-6b2c8a46f148"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Profile missing values by year\n",
    "temp_by_city['year'] = temp_by_city['dt'].dt.year\n",
    "missing_by_year = temp_by_city.groupby('year').apply(\n",
    "    lambda x: (x['AverageTemperature'].isna().sum() / len(x)) * 100\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize missing data pattern\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(missing_by_year.index, missing_by_year.values, color='orange', linewidth=2)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Missing Data (%)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Percentage of Missing Temperature Data by Year (Before Preparation)', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.axhline(y=50, color='red', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5, label='50% threshold')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Profile missing values by country (top 20 countries with most missing data)\n",
    "missing_by_country = temp_by_city.groupby('Country').apply(\n",
    "    lambda x: (x['AverageTemperature'].isna().sum() / len(x)) * 100\n",
    ").sort_values(ascending=False).head(20)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "plt.barh(range(len(missing_by_country)), missing_by_country.values, color='coral')\n",
    "plt.yticks(range(len(missing_by_country)), missing_by_country.index)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Missing Data (%)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Country', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Top 20 Countries by Missing Data Percentage', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='x')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "sWUuR12jJABo"
   },
   "source": [
    "The profiling reveals significant missing data in early historical records (pre-1900), with completeness improving substantially in the 20th century. Some countries exhibit higher missing value rates than others, which necessitates a robust imputation strategy during the preparation phase.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "KDpGsRx_JABo"
   },
   "source": [
    "#### Aggregation - Converting Monthly to Yearly Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Operation Type: Aggregation (Vertical Partitioning)\n",
    "\n",
    "We perform an aggregation operation to transform the monthly temperature records into yearly averages. This operation reduces the granularity of the temporal dimension from monthly to yearly, which aligns with our greenhouse gas emission data that is available at yearly resolution. By computing yearly means, we reduce data volume while preserving long-term climate trends essential for correlation analysis with emission patterns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "zXWThIwrJABo",
    "outputId": "bfdd2bb7-1792-4c68-b9d4-34376062f59f"
   },
   "outputs": [],
