  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ptJSrgZUJABo"
   },
   "source": [
    "#### Integration - Aggregating Cities to Countries Level\n",
    "\n",
    "Operations: Integration (Horizontal Aggregation)\n",
    "\n",
    "We perform an integration operation to roll up city-level temperature data to country-level averages. This transformation aligns the temperature data with our greenhouse gas emission data, which is available at country-level resolution. By computing weighted averages across all cities within each country, we create a unified dataset where both temperature and emission metrics share the same geographical granularity.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "Tebxm87JJABo",
    "outputId": "6fb9d7c6-75f6-44cc-e43e-df947905631d"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Aggregate city-level data to country-level yearly averages\n",
    "# We compute the mean temperature across all cities in each country for each year\n",
    "temp_country_yearly = temp_yearly.groupby(['Country', 'year']).agg({\n",
    "    'AverageTemperature': 'mean',\n",
    "    'City': 'count'  # Count number of cities contributing to each country-year\n",
    "}).rename(columns={'City': 'city_count'}).reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset shape after country-level aggregation: {temp_country_yearly.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nNumber of unique countries: {temp_country_yearly['Country'].nunique()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Year range: {temp_country_yearly['year'].min()} - {temp_country_yearly['year'].max()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSample of country-level yearly data:\")\n",
    "print(temp_country_yearly.head(160))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "CrpAhIipJABo"
   },
   "source": [
    "The integration operation successfully aggregates city-level variations into representative country-level temperature metrics. The black dashed line represents the country average, which smooths out local variations while capturing the overall national climate trend."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Cleaning - Filling Missing (country, year) Combinations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check number of combinations of (country, year)\n",
    "countries = temp_country_yearly['Country'].unique()\n",
    "years = temp_country_yearly['year'].unique()\n",
    "print(f\"Number of unique countries: {len(countries)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of unique years: {len(years)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Year range: {years.min()} - {years.max()}\")\n",
    "# Create full grid of (country, year) combinations\n",
    "full_grid = pd.MultiIndex.from_product(\n",
    "    [countries, years],\n",
    "    names=['Country', 'year']\n",
    ").to_frame(index=False)\n",
    "# Merge with actual data to find missing combinations\n",
    "merged = full_grid.merge(\n",
    "    temp_country_yearly[['Country', 'year']],\n",
    "    on=['Country', 'year'],\n",
    "    how='left',\n",
    "    indicator=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "missing_combinations = merged[merged['_merge'] == 'left_only'].drop(columns='_merge')\n",
    "expected_combinations = len(full_grid)\n",
    "actual_combinations = len(temp_country_yearly)\n",
    "missing_count = len(missing_combinations)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nExpected (country, year) combinations: {expected_combinations}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Actual (country, year) combinations:   {actual_combinations}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Missing (country, year) combinations:  {missing_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Coverage: {actual_combinations / expected_combinations * 100:.4f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot number of missing combinations by year\n",
    "missing_by_year = missing_combinations.groupby('year').size()\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(missing_by_year.index, missing_by_year.values, color='salmon')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Missing Country-Year Combinations', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Missing Country-Year Combinations by Year', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='y')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "From the plot, we can see that there are a lot of missing (country, year) combinations in the dataset, especially before 1850. We decide to cut off our analysis at 1850 to ensure we are working with a more complete dataset, while still capturing the long-term trends associated with industrialisation and greenhouse gas emissions. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "temp_country_yearly = temp_country_yearly[temp_country_yearly['year'] >= 1850]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We then fill the missing (country, year) combinations with NaN values, which will be imputed in the next step. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "countries = temp_country_yearly['Country'].unique()\n",
    "years = temp_country_yearly['year'].unique()\n",
    "print(f\"Number of unique countries: {len(countries)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of unique years: {len(years)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "full_grid = pd.MultiIndex.from_product(\n",
    "    [countries, years],\n",
    "    names=['Country', 'year']\n",
    ").to_frame(index=False)\n",
    "temp_country_yearly = full_grid.merge(\n",
    "    temp_country_yearly,\n",
    "    on=['Country', 'year'],\n",
    "    how='left'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "expected_combinations = len(full_grid)\n",
    "actual_combinations = len(temp_country_yearly)\n",
    "missing_count = expected_combinations - actual_combinations\n",
    "print(f\"Expected (country, year) combinations: {expected_combinations}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Actual (country, year) combinations:   {actual_combinations}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Missing (country, year) combinations:  {missing_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Coverage: {actual_combinations / expected_combinations * 100:.4f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "NDvQIfvuJABo"
   },
   "source": [
    "#### Cleaning - Filling up NaN values\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Imputation: Single-value imputation with known values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "0qEJk7aJJABo",
    "outputId": "16816fa0-f879-406a-a7dd-3c711199d7b8"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Before imputation - profile missing values\n",
    "print(\"Missing values BEFORE imputation:\")\n",
    "missing_before = temp_country_yearly['AverageTemperature'].isnull().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Total missing temperature values: {missing_before}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Percentage missing: {(missing_before / len(temp_yearly)) * 100:.2f}%\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Track which values are missing BEFORE we change them\n",
    "temp_country_yearly['was_imputed'] = temp_country_yearly['AverageTemperature'].isnull()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Sort the dataset (CRITICAL STEP)\n",
    "# We ensure the data is chronological for each Country\n",
    "temp_country_yearly = temp_country_yearly.sort_values(by=['Country', 'year'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Impute using linear interpolation\n",
    "# Group by Country, then interpolate to fill gaps in the timeline\n",
    "temp_country_yearly['AverageTemperature'] = temp_country_yearly.groupby(['Country'])['AverageTemperature'].transform(\n",
    "    lambda x: x.interpolate(method='linear', limit_direction='both')\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# After imputation - profile missing values\n",
    "print(\"Missing values AFTER imputation:\")\n",
    "missing_after = temp_country_yearly['AverageTemperature'].isnull().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Total missing temperature values: {missing_after}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Percentage missing: {(missing_after / len(temp_yearly)) * 100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of values successfully imputed: {missing_before - missing_after}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check if any NaNs remain\n",
    "if missing_after > 0:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nNote: {missing_after} values could not be interpolated (likely due to missing data at the start/end of a timeline, or consecutive gaps > 1 year).\")"
   ]
  },
