   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_path = ROOT + \"weather/\"\n",
    "weather = pd.read_parquet(data_path + \"daily_weather.parquet\")\n",
    "cities = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"cities.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cities_needed = cities[['station_id', 'city_name', 'country', 'iso3', 'latitude', 'longitude']]\n",
    "cities_needed = cities_needed.drop_duplicates(subset='station_id')\n",
    "cities_needed.set_index('station_id', inplace=True)\n",
    "for col in ['city_name', 'country', 'iso3', 'latitude', 'longitude']:\n",
    "    weather[col] = weather['station_id'].map(cities_needed[col])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "LWNTO0INJABp"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "weather.info()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We add country data to the weather dataset by merging the weather data with the cities data using the common column 'station_id'. This allows us to have country-level information associated with each weather record."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "5f_Wun1pJABp"
   },
   "source": [
    "Next, we will aggregate by year and country."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "UOpLnk2AJABp"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create year column\n",
    "weather['year'] = weather['date'].dt.year"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "dNpE_suvJABq"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "country_yearly = (\n",
    "    weather\n",
    "    .groupby(['country','year'])\n",
    "    .agg(\n",
    "        avg_temp_c=('avg_temp_c','mean'),\n",
    "        min_temp_c=('min_temp_c','min'),\n",
    "        max_temp_c=('max_temp_c','max'),\n",
    "        precipitation_mm=('precipitation_mm','mean'),\n",
    "        snow_depth_mm=('snow_depth_mm','mean'),\n",
    "        avg_wind_dir_deg=('avg_wind_dir_deg','mean'),\n",
    "        avg_wind_speed_kmh=('avg_wind_speed_kmh','mean'),\n",
    "        peak_wind_gust_kmh=('peak_wind_gust_kmh','max'),\n",
    "        avg_sea_level_pres_hpa=('avg_sea_level_pres_hpa','mean'),\n",
    "        sunshine_total_min=('sunshine_total_min','min'),\n",
    "        num_stations=('station_id','nunique')\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    .reset_index()\n",
    ")\n",
    "country_yearly"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We check for outliers in each of the weather attributes. This helps us identify any extreme values that may need to be handled before analysis. We see that snow depth and precipitation have some extreme values (around 10%), which can be consider normal for these attributes, as they can have significant variability. However, we will keep this in mind when performing our analysis and consider using robust statistical methods that are less sensitive to outliers if necessary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Outlier summary by numeric column (IQR method) + plot\n",
    "numeric_cols = country_yearly.select_dtypes(include=\"number\").columns\n",
    "\n",
    "outlier_stats = []\n",
    "for col in numeric_cols:\n",
    "    s = country_yearly[col].dropna()\n",
    "    if s.empty:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    q1, q3 = s.quantile([0.25, 0.75])\n",
    "    iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "\n",
    "    # If no spread, mark 0 outliers\n",
    "    if iqr == 0:\n",
    "        outlier_count = 0\n",
    "        outlier_percent = 0.0\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        lower = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "        upper = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "        outlier_count = ((s < lower) | (s > upper)).sum()\n",
    "        outlier_percent = outlier_count / len(s) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "    outlier_stats.append({\n",
    "        \"column\": col,\n",
    "        \"non_null_count\": len(s),\n",
    "        \"outlier_count\": int(outlier_count),\n",
    "        \"outlier_percent\": outlier_percent\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "outlier_df = pd.DataFrame(outlier_stats).sort_values(\"outlier_percent\", ascending=False)\n",
    "display(outlier_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "plt.barh(outlier_df[\"column\"], outlier_df[\"outlier_percent\"])\n",
    "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Outlier Percentage (%)\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Numeric Column\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Outlier Percentage by Weather Variable (IQR Method)\")\n",
    "plt.grid(axis=\"x\", alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "nIW6oA7WJABq"
   },
   "source": [
    "Plotting histogram to check for null values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "wni5yIgVJABq"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "null_counts = country_yearly.isnull().sum()\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "plt.bar(null_counts.index, (null_counts.values / len(country_yearly)) * 100)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Columns\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Number of Null Values (% of total)\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Histogram of Null Values per Column\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')  # Rotate x-axis labels for readability\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "There are a lot of null values in the datasets. Attributes that seem to be usable for our analysis are temperature and precipitation. We will drop other columns, since the number of null values is too high to be clean up."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ngFWIKTRJABq"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# drop extremely sparse columns\n",
    "country_yearly = country_yearly.drop(columns=[\n",
    "    'snow_depth_mm',\n",
    "    'avg_wind_dir_deg',\n",
    "    'avg_wind_speed_kmh',\n",
    "    'peak_wind_gust_kmh',\n",
    "    'avg_sea_level_pres_hpa',\n",
    "    'sunshine_total_min'\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# sort data first\n",
    "country_yearly = country_yearly.sort_values(['country','year'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# reconstruct avg temperature from min/max\n",
    "country_yearly['avg_temp_c'] = country_yearly['avg_temp_c'].fillna(\n",
    "    country_yearly[['min_temp_c','max_temp_c']].mean(axis=1)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# interpolate over time within each country\n",
    "cols = ['avg_temp_c','min_temp_c','max_temp_c','precipitation_mm']\n",
    "\n",
    "country_yearly[cols] = (\n",
    "    country_yearly\n",
    "    .groupby('country')[cols]\n",
    "    .transform(lambda x: x.interpolate(method='linear'))\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# fill remaining edges (first/last year)\n",
    "country_yearly[cols] = (\n",
    "    country_yearly\n",
    "    .groupby('country')[cols]\n",
    "    .transform(lambda x: x.ffill().bfill())\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We drop the columns with too many null values, and we did some missing value imputation for temperature and precipitation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "eqSmiHybJABq"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "country_yearly.info()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "However, we found another problem with the dataset, which is that some countries have very little data to offer. As we can see from the cell below, there are only 35 country available before 1900. This time range is not aligned with another datasets and will break our goal of long-term analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "country_yearly[country_yearly['year'] <= 1900]['country'].unique()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the end, we consider not using this dataset for our analysis, since the amount of missing data is too high and it will be hard to clean up."
   ]
  },
