   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "del weather\n",
    "gc.collect()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "gYUwLow4JABq"
   },
   "source": [
    "### DS3 & DS4 Preparation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### DS3 Structuring"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "As described in the data exploration section, we will choose to use fuel type as the main dimension for our analysis instead of sector, since there are too many sectors, which can increase a lot of complexity in our analysis. We will load country-level data by fuel type and do the same pivotting as before."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_path = ROOT + \"CEDS_v_2025_03_18_aggregate/\"\n",
    "bc = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"BC_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "ch4 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"CH4_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "co2 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"CO2_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "co = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"CO_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "n2o = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"N2O_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "nh3 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"NH3_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "nmvoc = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"NMVOC_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "nox = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"NOx_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "oc = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"OC_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")\n",
    "so2 = pd.read_csv(data_path + \"SO2_CEDS_estimates_by_country_v_2025_03_18.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dfs = [bc, ch4, co2, co, n2o, nh3, nmvoc, nox, oc, so2]\n",
    "long_dfs = []\n",
    "for df in dfs:\n",
    "    year_cols = [col for col in df.columns if col.startswith('X')]\n",
    "    df = df.drop(columns='units')\n",
    "    df_long = df.melt(id_vars=['em', 'country'],\n",
    "                      value_vars=year_cols,\n",
    "                      var_name='year', value_name='value')\n",
    "    df_long['year'] = df_long['year'].str[1:].astype(int)\n",
    "    long_dfs.append(df_long)\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3 = pd.concat(long_dfs, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3 = ds3.pivot_table(\n",
    "          index=['country', 'year'],\n",
    "          columns='em',\n",
    "          values='value'\n",
    "      ).reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "for gas in ds3.columns.difference(['country', 'year']):\n",
    "    ds3[gas] = ds3[gas].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We do the same pivotting as we did in data profiling to get the data in the format we want for our analysis, which is country, year and emission of each gas."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot percentage of missing values per gas over time\n",
    "gas_data = ds3.melt(id_vars=['country', 'year'], var_name='gas', value_name='emission')\n",
    "\n",
    "missing_by_gas_year = (\n",
    "    gas_data\n",
    "    .groupby(['gas', 'year'])['emission']\n",
    "    .apply(lambda x: ((x.isna()) | (x == 0)).mean() * 100)\n",
    "    .reset_index(name='missing_pct')\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n",
    "for gas in missing_by_gas_year['gas'].unique():\n",
    "    gas_subset = missing_by_gas_year[missing_by_gas_year['gas'] == gas]\n",
    "    plt.plot(gas_subset['year'], gas_subset['missing_pct'], label=gas, linewidth=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Missing Values (%)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Percentage of Missing Emission Data by Gas Over Time', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3 = ds3[ds3['year'] > 1850].copy()\n",
    "ds3 = ds3.reset_index(drop=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Looking at missing values in the datasets, we see that `CH4` and `N2O` have no data at all before around 1970s, which is likely due to lack of measurement. However, we have data from Our World in Data (DS4) since 1850, so we can use to fill in these missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "We also see that `CO2` which is the main greenhouse gas, has a lot of missing values before 1850s, so we will consider dropping all records before 1850s from our analysis to make CO2 data more complete and reliable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Try interpolation for every gas\n",
    "gases = ds3.columns.difference(['country', 'year', 'N2O', 'CH4']) \n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Missing values before interpolation:\")\n",
    "for gas in gases:\n",
    "    missing_count = ds3[gas].isna().sum()\n",
    "    print(f\"{gas}: {missing_count}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3[gases] = ds3.groupby(['country'])[gases].transform(\n",
    "    lambda x: x.interpolate(method='linear')\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nMissing values after interpolation:\")\n",
    "for gas in gases:\n",
    "    missing_count = ds3[gas].isna().sum()\n",
    "    print(f\"{gas}: {missing_count}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Looks like interpolating does not work well for CO2, as there are some countries with a lot of missing values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3[ds3['CO2'].isna()].groupby('country').size().sort_values(ascending=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We decide to leave the missing values as they are for now, and we will fill them with DS4 later. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Enriching by converting ISO3 code to country name"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We convert ISO3 codes to country names for merging with other datasets. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def alpha3_to_name(code):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        return pycountry.countries.get(alpha_3=code).name\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3['ISO3'] = ds3['country']\n",
    "ds3['country'] = ds3['ISO3'].apply(alpha3_to_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Find country that is None\n",
    "print(ds3[ds3['country'].isna()]['ISO3'].unique())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`global` is not a real country, so we will drop it from our analysis. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3 = ds3[ds3['ISO3'] != 'global'].reset_index(drop=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Cleaning by filling up missing values with DS4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "As we have seen from the data exploration section, there are large time periods with missing values for CH4 and N2O emissions in the CEDS dataset. To fill these gaps, we will use the global-level emissions data from Our World in Data (DS4), which provides comprehensive coverage of greenhouse gas emissions over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### DS4 Preprocessing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds4 = pd.read_csv(ROOT + \"ourworldindata-ghg/ghg_emissions_by_gas.csv\")\n",
    "ds4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds4.info()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We do some manipulation to ds4 to make it in the same format as ds3, including change of column names and converting units. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds4.rename(columns={\n",
    "    'annual_emissions_n2o_total_co2eq': 'N2O', \n",
    "    'annual_emissions_ch4_total_co2eq': 'CH4', \n",
    "    'annual_emissions_co2_total': 'CO2'}, inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Drop countries with all NaN values we found in data exploration section."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gas_cols = ['N2O', 'CH4', 'CO2']\n",
    "\n",
    "countries_with_nan = ds4.loc[ds4[gas_cols].isna().any(axis=1), 'entity'].unique()\n",
    "\n",
    "ds4 = ds4[~ds4['entity'].isin(countries_with_nan)].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dropped {len(countries_with_nan)} countries with NaN values.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Remaining countries: {ds4['entity'].nunique()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "DS4 also have ISO3 country code which we will use for merging with DS3. We have to check the null values in the `code` column first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check missing values in ds4 'code' column\n",
    "missing_code_count = ds4['code'].isna().sum()\n",
    "missing_code_pct = (missing_code_count / len(ds4)) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Missing values in 'code': {missing_code_count} ({missing_code_pct:.2f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ds4_missing_code = ds4[ds4['code'].isna()]\n",
    "print(\"\\nEntities with missing code:\")\n",
    "print(ds4_missing_code['entity'].unique())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Looks like null values in the `code` column are continents and groups of countries, which we will drop from our analysis since they are not real countries."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds4 = ds4[ds4['code'].notna()]\n",
    "ds4['code'] = ds4['code'].apply(lambda x: x.lower())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Converting units to match DS3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Since units given in ds4 are tonnes of CO2 equivalent, we will convert them using this formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "`tonnes of gas = tonnes of CO₂​ / GWP of the gas`\n",
    "\n",
    "GWP (Global Warming Potential) is a measure of how much heat a greenhouse gas traps in the atmosphere compared to CO2. Therefore, to convert from tonnes of CO2 equivalent to tonnes of the specific gas, we divide the CO2 equivalent emissions by the GWP of that gas. We choose to use 100-year GWP values from the IPCC Sixth Assessment Report, which are commonly used in climate change analysis. The GWP values we use for conversion are:\n",
    "- CH4: 28.4 (average of fossil and non-fossil)\n",
    "- N2O: 273"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds4['CH4'] = ds4['CH4'] / 28.4\n",
    "ds4['N2O'] = ds4['N2O'] / 273\n",
    "\n",
    "# to kilotonnes\n",
    "ds4['CH4'] = ds4['CH4'] / 1000 \n",
    "ds4['N2O'] = ds4['N2O'] / 1000 \n",
    "ds4['CO2'] = ds4['CO2'] / 1000"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Recheck year range of missing values for CH4 and N2O in DS3, which is around 1970s and before. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check peroid that ds3 missing CH4 and N2O data\n",
    "ds3_missing_ch4 = ds3[ds3['CH4'].isna()]\n",
    "ds3_missing_n2o = ds3[ds3['N2O'].isna()]\n",
    "print(\"DS3 missing CH4 data:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Year range: {ds3_missing_ch4['year'].min()} - {ds3_missing_ch4['year'].max()}\")\n",
    "print(\"DS3 missing N2O data:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Year range: {ds3_missing_n2o['year'].min()} - {ds3_missing_n2o['year'].max()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Comparing trends and filling missing values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We check how much existing data from both datasets align to confirm that source and values are consistent."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sample_country = 'China'\n",
    "gases = ['CH4', 'N2O']\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3_country = ds3[(ds3['country'] == sample_country) & (ds3['year'] >= 1970)]\n",
    "ds4_country = ds4[(ds4['entity'] == sample_country) & (ds4['year'] >= 1970)]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(14, 10), sharex=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, gas in enumerate(gases):\n",
    "    ax = axes[i]\n",
    "    ax.plot(ds3_country['year'], ds3_country[gas], label='DS3', linewidth=2)\n",
    "    ax.plot(ds4_country['year'], ds4_country[gas], label='DS4', linewidth=2)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'{gas} Emissions Over Time - {sample_country}')\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Emissions')\n",
    "    ax.legend()\n",
    "    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('Year')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compare DS3 vs DS4 for CH4 and N2O (1970-2023)\n",
    "comparison = (\n",
    "    ds3[['ISO3', 'year', 'CH4', 'N2O']]\n",
    "    .merge(\n",
    "        ds4[['code', 'year', 'CH4', 'N2O']],\n",
    "        left_on=['ISO3', 'year'],\n",
    "        right_on=['code', 'year'],\n",
    "        suffixes=('_ds3', '_ds4'),\n",
    "        how='inner'\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "comparison = comparison[(comparison['year'] >= 1970) & (comparison['year'] <= 2023)].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "results = {}\n",
    "for gas in ['CH4', 'N2O']:\n",
    "    ds3_vals = comparison[f'{gas}_ds3']\n",
    "    ds4_vals = comparison[f'{gas}_ds4']\n",
    "    diff = (ds3_vals - ds4_vals).dropna()\n",
    "    pct_diff = ((ds3_vals - ds4_vals) / ds4_vals.replace(0, np.nan) * 100).dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "    results[gas] = {\n",
    "        'n_pairs': len(diff),\n",
    "        'mean_absolute_error': diff.abs().mean(),          \n",
    "        'mean_absolute_percentage_error': pct_diff.abs().mean()  \n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "error_summary = pd.DataFrame(results).T\n",
    "print(\"Mean error summary (1970-2023):\")\n",
    "display(error_summary)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The emissions data from DS3 and DS4 align well for the overlapping years, with consistent trends and accurate values. This gives us confidence that using DS4 to fill missing values in DS3 is a valid approach, as both datasets appear to be reliable and compatible for our analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check how many country in ds3 and ds4 match\n",
    "ds3_countries = set(ds3['ISO3'].unique())\n",
    "ds4_countries = set(ds4['code'].unique())\n",
    "matching_countries = ds3_countries.intersection(ds4_countries)\n",
    "print(f\"Number of matching countries in DS3 and DS4: {len(matching_countries)}\")\n",
    "unmatched_countries_ds3 = ds3_countries - ds4_countries\n",
    "unmatched_countries_ds4 = ds4_countries - ds3_countries\n",
    "print(f\"Countries in DS3 but not in DS4: {unmatched_countries_ds3}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Countries in DS4 but not in DS3: {unmatched_countries_ds4}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We already have high number of countries in our dataset, so we will drop countries that are unmatched between the two datasets. Then, we performs a row-wise, conditional imputation of missing values in ds3 using aligned country-year data from ds4."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Drop unmatched countries from ds3\n",
    "ds3 = ds3[ds3['ISO3'].isin(matching_countries)].copy()  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Fill missing CH4 and N2O in ds3 with ds4 values for matching countries\n",
    "for gas in ['CH4', 'N2O', 'CO2']:\n",
    "    for country in matching_countries:\n",
    "        ds3_sub = ds3[(ds3['ISO3'] == country) & (ds3[gas].isna())]\n",
    "        ds4_sub = ds4[ds4['code'] == country].set_index('year')\n",
    "\n",
    "        for idx, row in ds3_sub.iterrows():\n",
    "            year = row['year']\n",
    "            if year in ds4_sub.index:\n",
    "                ds3.at[idx, gas] = ds4_sub.at[year, gas]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Finalize (country-level)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3_final = ds3.copy()\n",
    "print(\"Final DS3 profile:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Shape: {ds3_final.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unique countries: {ds3_final['country'].nunique()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Year range: {ds3_final['year'].min()} - {ds3_final['year'].max()}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nMissing values per column:\")\n",
    "print(ds3_final.isnull().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Global-level data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# aggregate into global\n",
    "ds3_global_final = ds3_final.groupby('year').agg({\n",
    "    'BC': 'sum',\n",
    "    'CH4': 'sum',\n",
    "    'CO': 'sum',\n",
    "    'CO2': 'sum',\n",
    "    'N2O': 'sum',\n",
    "    'NH3': 'sum',\n",
    "    'NMVOC': 'sum',\n",
    "    'NOx': 'sum',\n",
    "    'OC': 'sum',\n",
    "    'SO2': 'sum'\n",
    "}).reset_index()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3_global_final"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gases = ['BC','CH4','CO','N2O','NH3','NMVOC','NOx','OC','SO2']\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 7))\n",
    "for gas in gases:\n",
    "    plt.plot(ds3_global_final['year'], ds3_global_final[gas], label=gas, linewidth=2)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Emissions', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Global Emissions Over Time - Prepared DS3', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
