    "    - 1A4b_Residential (c)\n",
    "  - Commercial (RCOC)\n",
    "    - 1A4a_Commercial-institutional (c)\n",
    "  - Other (RCOO)\n",
    "    - 1A4c_Agriculture-forestry-fishing (c)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Solvents (SLV)\n",
    "  - 2D_Degreasing-Cleaning (p)\n",
    "  - 2D3_Other-product-use (p)\n",
    "  - 2D_Paint-application (p)\n",
    "  - 2D3_Chemical-products-manufacture-processing (p)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Agriculture (AGR)\n",
    "  - 3B_Manure-management (p)\n",
    "  - 3D_Soil-emissions (p)\n",
    "  - 3I_Agriculture-other (p)\n",
    "  - 3D_Rice-Cultivation (p)\n",
    "  - 3E_Enteric-fermentation (p)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Waste (WST)\n",
    "  - 5A_Solid-waste-disposal (p)\n",
    "  - 5E_Other-waste-handling (p)\n",
    "  - 5C_Waste-incineration (p)\n",
    "  - 5D_Wastewater-handling (p)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Shipping (SHP)\n",
    "  - 1A3di_International-shipping (c)\n",
    "  - 1A3di_Oil_Tanker_Loading (p)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We group the sectors into broader categories based on the details above, which is given in the CEDS paper. This grouping helps to reduce complexity in our analysis while still capturing the main sources of emissions across different sectors. By categorizing the sectors into Energy production, Industry, Transportation, Residential/commercial/other, Solvents, Agriculture, Waste, and Shipping, we can analyze emission trends by these broader categories and their impact on climate change."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def get_sector_group(sector):\n",
    "    if sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"1A1a_\", \"1A1bc_\", \"1B1_\", \"1B2_\", \"1B2d_\", \"7A_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Energy production\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"1A2a_\", \"1A2b_\", \"1A2c_\", \"1A2d_\", \"1A2e_\", \"1A2f_\", \"1A2g_\", \"1A5_\",\n",
    "        \"2A1_\", \"2A2_\", \"2A6_\", \"2B_\", \"2C_\", \"2H_\", \"2L_\", \"6A_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Industry\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"1A3b_\", \"1A3c_\", \"1A3dii_\", \"1A3eii_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Transportation\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"1A4b_\", \"1A4a_\", \"1A4c_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Residential, commercial, other\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"2D_\", \"2D3_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Solvents\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"3B_\", \"3D_\", \"3I_\", \"3E_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Agriculture\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"5A_\", \"5E_\", \"5C_\", \"5D_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Waste\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif sector.startswith((\n",
    "        \"1A3di_\"\n",
    "    )):\n",
    "        return \"Shipping\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return \"Other\"\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3_global['sector_group'] = ds3_global['sector'].apply(get_sector_group)\n",
    "ds3_global = ds3_global.groupby(['year', 'fuel', 'sector_group']).sum(numeric_only=True).reset_index()\n",
    "ds3_global.rename(columns={'sector_group': 'sector'}, inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "**CEDS fuels**\n",
    "\n",
    "Coal\n",
    "\n",
    "- Brown coal\n",
    "- Coal coke\n",
    "- Hard coal\n",
    "\n",
    "Biofuel\n",
    "- Biofuel\n",
    "\n",
    "Liquid fuel and natural gas\n",
    "- Heavy oil\n",
    "- Diesel oil\n",
    "- Light oil\n",
    "- Natural Gas\n",
    "\n",
    "Process\n",
    "- Process"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We group fuels into broader categories based on the details above, which is given in the CEDS paper. This grouping helps to reduce complexity in our analysis while still capturing the main sources of emissions across different fuel types. By categorizing the fuels into Coal, Biofuel, Liquid fuel and natural gas, and Process, we can analyze emission trends by these broader categories and their impact on climate change."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def get_fuel_group(fuel):\n",
    "    if fuel in ['brown_coal', 'coal_coke', 'hard_coal']:\n",
    "        return 'coal'\n",
    "    elif fuel in ['diesel_oil', 'heavy_oil', 'light_oil', 'natural_gas']:\n",
    "        return 'oil_gas'\n",
    "    elif fuel in ['biomass']:\n",
    "        return 'biomass'\n",
    "    elif fuel in ['process']:\n",
    "        return 'process'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'other'\n",
    "\n",
    "ds3_global['fuel_group'] = ds3_global['fuel'].apply(get_fuel_group)\n",
    "ds3_global = ds3_global.groupby(['year', 'sector', 'fuel_group']).sum(numeric_only=True).reset_index()\n",
    "ds3_global.rename(columns={'fuel_group': 'fuel'}, inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3_global"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gas_cols = [c for c in ds3_global.columns if c not in ['year', 'sector', 'fuel']]\n",
    "\n",
    "nan_mask = ds3_global[gas_cols].isna()\n",
    "zero_mask = ds3_global[gas_cols] == 0\n",
    "total_values = ds3_global[gas_cols].size\n",
    "\n",
    "total_nan = nan_mask.sum().sum()\n",
    "total_zero = zero_mask.sum().sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Overall\")\n",
    "print(\"Total NaN values:\", total_nan)\n",
    "print(f\"NaN ratio: {total_nan / total_values:.2%}\")\n",
    "print(\"Total 0 values:\", total_zero)\n",
    "print(f\"0 ratio: {total_zero / total_values:.2%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nAfter 1850\")\n",
    "ds3_post1850 = ds3_global[ds3_global['year'] >= 1850]\n",
    "total_values_post1850 = ds3_post1850[gas_cols].size\n",
    "\n",
    "nan_mask_post1850 = ds3_post1850[gas_cols].isna()\n",
    "zero_mask_post1850 = ds3_post1850[gas_cols] == 0\n",
    "\n",
    "total_nan_post1850 = nan_mask_post1850.sum().sum()\n",
    "total_zero_post1850 = zero_mask_post1850.sum().sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Total NaN values:\", total_nan_post1850)\n",
    "print(f\"NaN ratio: {total_nan_post1850 / total_values_post1850:.2%}\")\n",
    "print(\"Total 0 values:\", total_zero_post1850)\n",
    "print(f\"0 ratio: {total_zero_post1850 / total_values_post1850:.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We see that data after 1850 is more complete, so we will consider dropping records before 1850 to make our analysis more reliable. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Missing Data Count per Sector for Each Fuel\n",
    "missing_by_sector_fuel = (\n",
    "    ds3_global\n",
    "    .groupby(['sector', 'fuel'])[gas_cols]\n",
    "    .apply(lambda x: (x.isna() | x == 0).sum())\n",
    "    .reset_index()\n",
    ")\n",
    "# Plotting Missing Data Count by Sector and Fuel\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n",
    "for fuel in ds3_global['fuel'].unique():\n",
    "    subset = missing_by_sector_fuel[missing_by_sector_fuel['fuel'] == fuel]\n",
    "    plt.bar(subset['sector'], subset[gas_cols].sum(axis=1), label=fuel)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Sector', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count of Missing Values', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Count of Missing Emission Values by Sector and Fuel', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(axis='y', alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can see that missing data per sector for each fuel is very simple, with each sectors missing for 1-2 fuels, which is consistent with the fact that some sectors only use certain fuels. This means that we can still use this dataset for our analysis, since the missing data is not random and we can account for it in our analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3_global.to_csv(ROOT + \"ds3_global_sector_fuel.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### DS5 Preparation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sea_data = pd.read_csv(ROOT + \"ourworldindata-sea/sea_level.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Aggregation to yearly data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Transformation 1: We are going to create a Year column derived from the Day column, to match our objective of doing yearly analysis, as well as matching the other datasets that provide yearly data. Afterwards, we remove the Day column."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sea_data['day'] = pd.to_datetime(sea_data['day'])\n",
    "sea_data['year'] = sea_data['day'].dt.year"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sea_data.drop(columns=['day'], inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sea_data.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Transformation 2: We are grouping the data by Year and then getting the average. This will result in a dataset that shows the total mean sea level from the years 1880 to 2020. We can then merge this dataset with our other datasets using the Year column as the key."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "grouped = sea_data.groupby('year')['sea_level_average'].mean()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds5_final = grouped.reset_index().rename(columns= {'sea_level_average': 'Mean Sea Level'})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Final DS Merging"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Country-level data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Structuring and Merging prepared DSs by country "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We merge all prepared datasets together by country to create a comprehensive dataset that combines temperature and greenhouse gas emissions data for our analysis. This final dataset will allow us to explore correlations between emissions and weather patterns at the country level over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds1_final"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds3_final"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Merge ONLY countries that exist in both datasets\n",
    "merged = ds1_final.merge(ds3_final, on=['country', 'year'], how='inner')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find unmatched countries (for debugging)\n",
    "unmatched_ds1 = ds1_final[~ds1_final['country'].isin(ds3_final['country'])]['country'].unique()\n",
    "unmatched_ds3 = ds3_final[~ds3_final['country'].isin(ds1_final['country'])]['country'].unique()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Countries in DS1 but not in DS3:\")\n",
    "print(sorted(unmatched_ds1))\n",
    "print(f\"Total: {len(unmatched_ds1)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCountries in DS3 but not in DS1:\")\n",
    "print(sorted(unmatched_ds3))\n",
    "print(f\"Total: {len(unmatched_ds3)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMerged dataset shape: {merged.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Countries successfully matched: {merged['country'].nunique()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Some countries in the datasets have different names, so we will need to standardise the country names before merging. We will manually convert all country names to a standard format (ISO3 codes in this case) to ensure consistency across datasets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "country_mapping = {\n",
    "    \"Bolivia\": \"Bolivia, Plurinational State of\",\n",
    "    \"Bosnia And Herzegovina\": \"Bosnia and Herzegovina\",\n",
    "    \"Burma\": \"Myanmar\",\n",
    "    \"Congo (Democratic Republic Of The)\": \"Congo, The Democratic Republic of the\",\n",
    "    \"Czech Republic\": \"Czechia\",\n",
    "    \"Côte D'Ivoire\": \"Côte d'Ivoire\",\n",
    "    \"Guinea Bissau\":\"Guinea-Bissau\",\n",
    "    \"Iran\": \"Iran, Islamic Republic of\",\n",
    "    \"Laos\": \"Lao People's Democratic Republic\",\n",
    "    \"Macedonia\": \"North Macedonia\",  \n",
    "    \"Moldova\": \"Moldova, Republic of\",\n",
    "    \"Reunion\": \"Réunion\",\n",
    "    \"Russia\": \"Russian Federation\",\n",
    "    \"South Korea\": \"Korea, Republic of\",\n",
    "    \"Swaziland\": \"Eswatini\",\n",
    "    \"Syria\": \"Syrian Arab Republic\",\n",
    "    \"Taiwan\": \"Taiwan, Province of China\",\n",
    "    \"Tanzania\": \"Tanzania, United Republic of\",\n",
    "    \"Turkey\": \"Türkiye\",\n",
    "    \"Venezuela\":\"Venezuela, Bolivarian Republic of\",\n",
    "    \"Vietnam\": \"Viet Nam\",\n",
    "}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds1_mapped = ds1_final.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "ds1_mapped['country'] = ds1_mapped['country'].replace(country_mapping)\n",
    "\n",
    "merged = ds1_mapped.merge(ds3_final, on=['country', 'year'], how='inner')\n",
    "\n",
    "unmatched_ds1_after = ds1_mapped[~ds1_mapped['country'].isin(ds3_final['country'])]['country'].unique()\n",
    "unmatched_ds3_after = ds3_final[~ds3_final['country'].isin(ds1_mapped['country'])]['country'].unique()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Merged dataset shape: {merged.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Countries successfully matched: {merged['country'].nunique()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCountries in DS1 but not in DS3 (after mapping):\")\n",
    "print(sorted(unmatched_ds1_after))\n",
    "print(f\"Total: {len(unmatched_ds1_after)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCountries in DS3 but not in DS1 (after mapping):\")\n",
    "print(sorted(unmatched_ds3_after))\n",
    "print(f\"Total: {len(unmatched_ds3_after)}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Enriching by adding continent data for each country"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We use pycountry_convert library to get continent data for each country in our merged dataset. This will allow us to analyze regional patterns in emissions and weather data, and potentially identify differences between continents in our subsequent analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def iso3_to_continent(iso3):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        country = pycountry.countries.get(alpha_3=iso3)\n",
    "        if not country:\n",
    "            return None\n",
    "        country_alpha2 = country.alpha_2\n",
    "        continent_code = pc.country_alpha2_to_continent_code(country_alpha2)\n",
    "        continent_name = pc.convert_continent_code_to_continent_name(continent_code)\n",
    "        return continent_name\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "# Map the dictionary to your dataframe to create the new column\n",
    "merged['continent'] = merged['ISO3'].apply(lambda x: iso3_to_continent(x.upper()))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check for any unmapped countries \n",
    "unmapped_countries = merged[merged['continent'].isna()]['country'].unique()\n",
    "print(f\"Countries that could not be mapped to a continent: {unmapped_countries}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Enriching by adding location data for each country"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We use data from DS6 to get the latitude and longitude for each country in our merged dataset. This allows us to use the geographical information for spatial analysis and training machine learning models that may benefit from location data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds6 = pd.read_csv(ROOT + \"latlon/longitude-latitude.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds6 = ds6[['ISO-ALPHA-3','WikiData_Latitude','WikiData_Longitude']]\n",
    "ds6.rename(columns={\n",
    "    'ISO-ALPHA-3': 'ISO3',\n",
    "    'WikiData_Latitude': 'latitude',\n",
    "    'WikiData_Longitude': 'longitude'\n",
    "}, inplace=True)\n",
    "ds6.dropna(inplace=True)\n",
    "ds6['ISO3'] = ds6['ISO3'].apply(lambda x: x.lower())\n",
    "ds6 = ds6.drop_duplicates(subset='ISO3')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "final = merged.merge(ds6[['ISO3','latitude','longitude']], on='ISO3', how='left')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "final.info()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We merged this location data with our final country-level dataset using the ISO3 country codes as the key."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "final.to_csv(ROOT + \"final_country_ds.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
