    "An analysis of the top five most volatile countries reveals that temperature volatility is not uniform across geography or time. The data demonstrates a clear divide between historical, event-driven volatility in tropical regions and persistent, atmospheric-driven volatility in high-latitude regions, all of which are currently being overlaid by a modern anthropogenic warming trend.\n",
