   "source": [
    "From our table summary and the graph above, we observe a clear progression.\n",
    "\n",
    "Emissions are at their historical baseline and temperatures are below the 20th century average during the Industrial Acceleration era. Moving on, the War and Disruption era shows mixed signals, which can be explained by how wars disrupted the industrial progress/output and also expanded significantly on weapons production.\n",
    "\n",
    "Post-War Boom era is clearly a turning point. All the emissions surge simultaneously. This is the start of the sustained upward trajectory of temperature, with of course a lag of around 1 or 2 decades relative to emissions surge (lag effect).\n",
    "\n",
