   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gas_cols"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Predictive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Regression Models"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Even though we working with time series data, we shall trying out regression models to see if we can predict the average temperature based on the emissions data.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will evaluate the performance of the regression models through the following metrics:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **RMSE** (Root Mean Squared Error): Measures the average magnitude of the errors between predicted and actual values. A lower RMSE indicates better model performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **MAE** (Mean Absolute Error): Measures the average absolute difference between predicted and actual values. A lower MAE indicates better model performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **R²** (Coefficient of Determination): Measures the proportion of the variance in the dependent variable that is predictable from the independent variables. An R² value of 1 indicates a perfect fit, while a value of 0 indicates no linear relationship."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Feature Engineering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Feature engineering is a critical step in building effective models, especially when working with complex datasets that include multiple variables and potential interactions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = ds_country.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Year squared feature for non-linear trends\n",
    "df[\"year_squared\"] = df[\"year\"] ** 2\n",
    "\n",
    "# Total emissions\n",
    "df[\"total_emissions\"] = df[gas_cols].sum(axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort by country and year for lag features\n",
    "df = df.sort_values([\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Lag features for emissions\n",
    "lags = [1, 2, 3]  # Lag features\n",
    "for gas in gas_cols:\n",
    "    for lag in lags:\n",
    "        df[f\"{gas}_lag{lag}\"] = df.groupby(\"country\")[gas].shift(lag)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cumulative emissions by country\n",
    "for gas in gas_cols:\n",
    "    df[f\"{gas}_cumulative\"] = df.groupby(\"country\")[gas].cumsum()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop rows with NaN from lags\n",
    "df = df.dropna()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We did some feature engineering to create new features that can help us in our predictive analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Year Squared: This feature captures potential non-linear trends in temperature over time, as the relationship between year and temperature may not be strictly linear.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Total Emissions: This feature aggregates the total emissions across all gases, providing a single metric that may correlate strongly with temperature changes.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Lagged Emissions: This feature captures the emissions of each gas from the previous year, which may have a delayed effect on temperature changes.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Cumulative Emissions: This feature sums emissions of each gas over time, reflecting the cumulative impact of greenhouse gases on temperature"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Train-test split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Since this is a time series dataset, we will use a time-based train-test split. We will use the data from first 80% of the years as our training set, and the data from the remaining 20% of the years as our test set. This allows us to train our models on historical data and evaluate their performance on more recent data. We also scale the features using StandardScaler to ensure that all features are on the same scale, which can improve the performance of many machine learning algorithms."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "years = np.sort(df['year'].unique())\n",
    "split_idx = int(len(years) * 0.8)\n",
    "train_years = years[:split_idx]\n",
    "test_years = years[split_idx:]\n",
    "\n",
    "train_df = df[df['year'].isin(train_years)]\n",
    "test_df = df[df['year'].isin(test_years)]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop non-feature columns\n",
    "drop_cols = ['AvgTemp', 'ISO3', 'country', 'continent']\n",
    "X_train = train_df.drop(columns=drop_cols)\n",
    "y_train = train_df['AvgTemp']\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = test_df.drop(columns=drop_cols)\n",
    "y_test = test_df['AvgTemp']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scale features for better model performance and interpretability of coefficients\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "X_train_scaled = pd.DataFrame(X_train_scaled, columns=X_train.columns, index=X_train.index)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = pd.DataFrame(X_test_scaled, columns=X_test.columns, index=X_test.index)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Trains years:\", train_df['year'].min(), \"-\", train_df['year'].max())\n",
    "print(\"Test years:\", test_df['year'].min(), \"-\", test_df['year'].max())\n",
    "print(\"Training samples:\", len(train_df))\n",
    "print(\"Testing samples:\", len(test_df))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train_scaled"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
