   "source": [
    "##### Random Forest Regression"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Random Forest Regressor is a powerful ensemble learning method that can capture complex non-linear relationships between features and the target variable. By averaging the predictions of multiple decision trees, it reduces overfitting and improves generalization performance. The model's ability to handle high-dimensional data and capture interactions between features makes it well-suited for our analysis of temperature and emissions data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Training can be time-consuming, especially with a large dataset and many trees. You can expect 1-3 minutes running this in a normal Google Colab environment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def train_rf(X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test):\n",
    "    model = RandomForestRegressor(\n",
    "        n_estimators=50,\n",
    "        max_depth=10,\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        n_jobs=-1,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "    preds = model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    rmse = mean_squared_error(y_test, preds)\n",
    "    mae = mean_absolute_error(y_test, preds)\n",
    "    r2 = r2_score(y_test, preds)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    imp_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "        \"feature\": X_train.columns,\n",
    "        \"importance\": model.feature_importances_\n",
    "    }).sort_values(by=\"importance\", key=abs, ascending=False)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return model, rmse, mae, r2, imp_df\n",
    "\n",
    "# Full model \n",
    "rf_full, rmse_full, mae_full, r2_full, imp_full = train_rf(X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop all lag features\n",
    "lag_cols = [c for c in X_train.columns if \"_lag\" in c]\n",
    "X_train_no_lag = X_train.drop(columns=lag_cols)\n",
    "X_test_no_lag = X_test.drop(columns=lag_cols)\n",
    "rf_no_lag, rmse_no_lag, mae_no_lag, r2_no_lag, imp_no_lag = train_rf(X_train_no_lag, y_train, X_test_no_lag, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop cumulative features\n",
    "cumulative_cols = [c for c in X_train.columns if \"_cumulative\" in c]\n",
    "X_train_no_cum = X_train.drop(columns=cumulative_cols)\n",
    "X_test_no_cum = X_test.drop(columns=cumulative_cols)\n",
    "rf_no_cum, rmse_no_cum, mae_no_cum, r2_no_cum, imp_no_cum = train_rf(X_train_no_cum, y_train, X_test_no_cum, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop lag and cumulative features\n",
    "X_train_no_lag_cum = X_train.drop(columns=lag_cols + cumulative_cols)\n",
    "X_test_no_lag_cum = X_test.drop(columns=lag_cols + cumulative_cols)\n",
    "rf_no_lag_cum, rmse_no_lag_cum, mae_no_lag_cum, r2_no_lag_cum, imp_no_lag_cum = train_rf(X_train_no_lag_cum, y_train, X_test_no_lag_cum, y_test)"
   ]
  },
