    "##### Feature Importance Analysis with SHAP"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) is a powerful tool for interpreting the predictions of complex machine learning models, such as LSTMs. It provides a way to quantify the contribution of each feature to the model's predictions, allowing us to understand which emissions are most influential in driving temperature changes according to the model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_batch = []\n",
    "for X, y in test_loader:\n",
    "    X_batch.append(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = torch.cat(X_batch, dim=0)\n",
    "background = X_test[:100]\n",
    "test_data = X_test[:50]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We use SHAP with our trained LSTM model to compute the SHAP values for each feature, which represent the contribution of each feature to the predicted temperature. We then calculate the mean absolute SHAP value for each feature across all samples to determine their overall importance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model.to('cpu')\n",
    "explainer = shap.GradientExplainer(model, background)\n",
    "shap_values = explainer.shap_values(test_data)\n",
    "importance = shap_values.mean(axis=0).mean(axis=0)\n",
    "abs_importance = np.abs(importance)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
