    "### Prescriptive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This is continuation of the predictive section."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Predicting Future Temperature Under Emission Scenarios"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "COUNTRY = \"Singapore\"\n",
    "n_future = 20\n",
    "df_country = df[df['country'] == COUNTRY].sort_values('year').copy()\n",
    "last_year    = df_country['year'].max()\n",
    "future_years = np.arange(last_year + 1, last_year + n_future + 1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Future emissions are projected by compounding an annual growth rate derived from two components: the median year-over-year growth rate across the full historical period (long-run stability) and the median year-over-year growth rate over the most recent 10 years (recent momentum), blended at equal 50/50 weight. Using the median instead of the mean makes the rate robust to extreme spikes in early historical data. The blended rate is then applied as a fixed compound growth rate to simulate emissions over the forecast horizon."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def forecast_emissions_blend(series, steps, recent_years=20, w_recent=0.5):\n",
    "    yoy_all      = np.diff(series) / np.where(series[:-1] == 0, 1e-9, series[:-1])\n",
    "    rate_longrun = max(np.median(yoy_all), 0)   \n",
    "\n",
    "    series_recent = series[-recent_years:]\n",
    "    yoy_recent    = np.diff(series_recent) / np.where(series_recent[:-1] == 0, 1e-9, series_recent[:-1])\n",
    "    rate_recent   = max(np.median(yoy_recent), 0)  \n",
    "\n",
    "    blended_rate = w_recent * rate_recent + (1 - w_recent) * rate_longrun\n",
    "\n",
    "    last_val = series[-1]\n",
    "    forecast = []\n",
    "    for _ in range(steps):\n",
    "        last_val = last_val * (1 + blended_rate)\n",
    "        forecast.append(last_val)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return np.array(forecast), blended_rate, rate_recent, rate_longrun\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{'Gas':<8} {'Long-run':>10} {'Recent':>10} {'Blended':>10}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 42)\n",
    "\n",
    "gas_forecasts = {}\n",
    "growth_rates  = {}\n",
